# Line endings
#
# The repo was mixed: most files were stored LF, but a handful (styles/base.css,
# tokens.css, buttons.css, models.css, system.css, server/src/routes/settings.js)
# were stored CRLF. Nothing chose that — it is an accident of which editor last
# wrote each file on Windows. The cost is real: touching one of those files with
# a tool that writes LF rewrites EVERY line, so a ten-line change arrives as a
# two-thousand-line diff and the actual edit becomes unreviewable.
#
# So: normalize to LF in the repository. Working copies are unaffected on
# Windows as long as core.autocrlf is left at its default `true` — Git converts
# on checkout — and editors here handle LF regardless.
#
# This was applied once with `git add --renormalize .`, which is why the commit
# introducing this file also rewrites those six.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary types, declared ahead of need. There are none tracked today, but
# avatars and expression art are filesystem-stored and could plausibly land
# here later; a normalized PNG is a corrupted PNG, and it is much cheaper to
# say so now than to debug it then.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.db    binary
*.sqlite binary
